    <div class="content-text">
      <h3>Aims of WHCRG as a resilience hub</h3>
      We will endeavour to:
      <ol class="points-list">
        <li>
          To open the hall as a 'safe refuge' providing heat, light and phone
          charging facilities for West/mur community and anyone visiting.
        </li>
        <li>
          To maintain contact with the Angus Council Resilience Officer
          throughout any emergency.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use the hall as a receiving/distribution centre for equipment/supplies
          during an emergency.
        </li>
        <li>
          Provide a localised hub for use by the emergency services/utility
          companies in time of emergency.
        </li>
        <li>
          Address the wellbeing of those in the community who are most
          vulnerable.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h3>Opening the resilience hub</h3>

      WHCRG will try to open Westmuir Hall as a Resilience Hub under the
      following circumstances:
      <ol class="points-list">
        <li>
          There is a specific request made to open the hub by Angus Council
          Resilience Team.
        </li>
        <li>
          There is a specific request to open the hub by one or more of the
          emergency services (police, fire, ambulance).
        </li>
        <li>
          There is a specific request to open the hub by one or more of the
          utility companies (gas, water, electricity).
        </li>
        <li>
          WHCRG committee become aware of a serious situation that will affect
          the community but there has been no specific request made by any of
          the above to open the Resilience Hub.
        </li>
      </ol>

      When dealing with an incident or emergency WHCRG volunteers must not take
      unacceptable risks that place themselves or others in danger.
      <p>
        Further advice and Information can be found online at
        <a href="https://www.readyscotland.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >www.readyscotland.org</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
